# sphere_formtool.cam — camp-2 custom-tool-profile finishing fixture (ROADMAP
# Phase 3 "Custom tool/cutter profiles from SVG").
# Finishes the upper hemisphere of a Sphere with a FormTool carrying a
# tool_profile.svg profile instead of a Ballmill, using the vertex-following
# contact math in ops::finish::finish_sphere_profile (DECISIONS.md "Custom
# tool-profile finishing: vertex-following contact math, sphere first").
#
# tool_profile.svg (pre-scale, dia=10 -> scale factor 5): tip (0,0) -> corner
# (1,1) -> wall-top (1,2), scaling to (0,0) -> (5,5) -> (5,10) -- a 45 deg
# segment (tip->corner) followed by a vertical (90 deg) wall segment.
#
# Contained and paired since Phase 10 lane B, slice 0 (DECISIONS.md "Phase 10
# lane B, slice 0..."): the stock holds the dome (top z=10, 25mm below the
# equator plane) and T2 roughs the moat around it first, leaving 0.5mm for
# T1 -- sphere_clear.cam's own Clear, numbers and all. Until then the dome
# stood 10mm proud of a z=0 stock, because the form tool alone, contained,
# rejected at the SURROUND: the full stock beside the rim that nothing had
# roughed (standing stock at (48.819, 20.000, 9.839), its shank in the
# stock's top; the flat collar's day-one reading of (45.044, 20.000, 5.044)
# was the collar's own box-top). The program emits
# silent under every lint and gate, and its rest report claims 63 cells
# (~3.8 mm^3) of the pointed tip's ridges at the pole and nothing beside the
# rim: the claim there is the swept TUBE of the cutting form (lane B's
# slice 1), which replaced a flat collar that had called ~1289 mm^3 of air
# a 45-degree cone never enters removed. rapid_z clears the stock top (z=10).
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 15
clearance_z 30
spindle 4000

stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=35, x=0, y=0, z=10)

tool T2 Endmill(dia=12.0)
tool T1 FormTool(dia=10.0, profile="tool_profile.svg")

# Sphere centre (equator plane) at z=0; the machinable dome rises to z=10 (r=10).
feature TopDome Sphere(dia=20, x=30, y=20, z=0)

# stepover here is the Z pass spacing (waterline stepdown), same as the
# Ballmill sphere.cam fixture.
run Clear(tool=T2, profile=TopDome, stepover=8.0, stepdown=5.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run Form(tool=T1, surface=TopDome, stepover=3.0)
